40151" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507413 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507413 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the constant $b$ that makes the function $h(x)$ below continuous at $x=1.$\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{bx}, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-2, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507413 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d9d26f9-9e30-5030-aa28-1b26a93e7605" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507413 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=1,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}{e}^{bx} \\\\  & ={e}^{b(1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{b},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(3{x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =3(1)^{2}-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $h(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}h(x) \\\\ {e}^{b} & =1 \\\\ {e}^{b} & ={e}^{0} \\\\ b & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507427 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507427 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507427 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507427 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-b), & 2<x\\le 4 \\\\ 4-x, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nis continuous at  $x=4,$ find the value of $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507427 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "43cb36a7-f5a0-5d8b-b50f-29e51a864367" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507427 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=4,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}g(x) & =g(4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{2}-b) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-b),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}(4-x) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=4,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}g(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-b) & =0 \\\\ 2-b & =1 \\\\ b & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507439 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507439 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340360" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507439 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507439 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x-b}, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 4x-2, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis continuous at $x=1,$ find the value of the constant $b.$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507439 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55ddc220-8d66-534a-9802-0f8e226d8a1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507439 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=1,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\sqrt{x-b} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1-b},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(4x-2) \\\\  & =4(1)-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x) \\\\ \\sqrt{1-b} & =2 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{1-b})}^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ 1-b & =4 \\\\ b & =1-4 \\\\ b & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507443 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340183" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507443 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507443 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}\\,(x+{b}^{2}), & x\\le 3 \\\\ x-1, & x>3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nis continuous at  $x=3,$  find the possible values of $b.$\n\nArranged in **ascending order**,\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,b=$\n\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507443 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6259a4b8-da5e-572e-ac26-51a1c1822402" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507443 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=3,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}{log}_{2}\\,(x+{b}^{2})={log}_{2}\\,(3+{b}^{2}),\n$$\n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}(x-1)=3-1=2.\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=3,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}g(x) \\\\ {log}_{2}\\,(3+{b}^{2}) & =2 \\\\ 3+{b}^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ 3+{b}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {b}^{2} & =1 \\\\ b & =-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function is continuous at $x=3$ for the values\n\n$$\nb=-1\\,\\text{and}\\,b=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507447 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507447 #edb/ref 1069 "q-4590" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507447 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507447 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the values of the constants $a$ and $b$ that make the function $g(x)$ below continuous at $x=-2$ and $x=0.$\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x, & x\\le -2 \\\\ a{x}^{2}+b, & -2<x<0 \\\\ 6, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507447 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "73018209-5cd9-51f0-b7f1-6d1df6445523" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507447 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=-2,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}g(x) & =g(-2) \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}(a{x}^{2}+b) \\\\  & =a(-2)^{2}+b \\\\  & =4a+b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-2,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}g(x) \\\\ 2 & =4a+b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, at $x=0,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(a{x}^{2}+b) \\\\  & =a(0)^{2}+b \\\\  & =0+b \\\\  & =b,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}g(x) & =g(0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}g(x) \\\\ b & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's solve the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4a+b=2 \\\\ b=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can replace $b$ by $6$ in the first equation. Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+b & =2 \\\\ 4a+6 & =2 \\\\ 4a & =-4 \\\\ a & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2$ and $x=0$ for $a=-1$ and $b=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507451 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507451 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108030" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507451 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507451 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2x+1}, & x<4 \\\\ ax, & x\\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis continuous at $x=4,$ find the value of the constant $a.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507451 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "791bb302-4274-58d7-bd6c-ad45a6412218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507451 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=4,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\sqrt{2x+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2(4)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}g(x) & =g(4)=4a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=4,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}g(x) \\\\ 3 & =4a \\\\ a & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507453 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507453 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507453 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507453 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the constant $c$ that makes the function $h(x)$ below continuous at $x=1.$\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{4}^{cx}\\,\\,, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 6x+10, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507453 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81da8b9c-598f-5273-b4fb-93dfa4451ef0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507453 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=1,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}h(x) & =h(1) \\\\  & ={4}^{c(1)} \\\\  & ={4}^{c},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(6x+10) \\\\  & =6(1)+10 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $h(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{c} & =16 \\\\ {4}^{c} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ c & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$ for $c=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-48580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507459 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the constant $b$ that make the function $g(x)$ below continuous at $x=1.$\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2, & x\\le 1 \\\\ {b}^{2}+2xb, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "928df4f7-9920-5d89-a736-8ebd227a0dd7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507459 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=1,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x) & =g(1) \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}({b}^{2}+2xb) \\\\  & ={b}^{2}+2(1)b \\\\  & ={b}^{2}+2b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x) \\\\ -1 & ={b}^{2}+2b \\\\ {b}^{2}+2b+1 & =0 \\\\ (b+1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{(b+1)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |b+1| & =0 \\\\ b & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$ for $b=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507460 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507460 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108026" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507460 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507460 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x+1}, & x\\le 8 \\\\ ax+2, & x>8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis continuous at $x=8,$ find the value of the constant $a.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507460 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "98316fee-a245-5ddf-ac9f-eeeebb819420" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507460 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=8,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {8}^{-}}g(x) & =g(8) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {8}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {8}^{+}}(ax+2) \\\\  & =8a+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=8,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {8}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {8}^{+}}g(x) \\\\ 3 & =8a+2 \\\\ 8a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507465 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507465 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108127" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507465 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507465 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+a), & -6\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ x-1, & x>