={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}{2}^{bx} \\\\  & ={2}^{b(2)} \\\\  & ={2}^{2b},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}({x}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =(2)^{2}+4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $h(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}h(x) \\\\ {2}^{2b} & =8 \\\\ {2}^{2b} & ={2}^{3} \\\\ 2b & =3 \\\\ b & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507493 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507493 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37914" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507493 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507493 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the constant $k$ that make the function $f(x)$ below continuous at $x=-1.$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}k{x}^{2}+5x-2k, & x\\le -1 \\\\ 4x+3, & x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507493 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bfc91a1b-1b4d-56a2-b2c1-01651ff7abbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507493 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=-1,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x) & =f(-1) \\\\  & =k{(-1)}^{2}+5(-1)-2k \\\\  & =k-5-2k \\\\  & =-k-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}(4x+3) \\\\  & =4(-1)+3 \\\\  & =-4+3 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-1,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}f(x) \\\\ -k-5 & =-1 \\\\ -k & =4 \\\\ k & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$ for $k=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507502 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507502 #edb/ref 1069 "q-339925" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507502 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] 